The _[ residence time ](/wiki/Residence_time "Residence time") _ of [ water
](/wiki/Water "Water") is a key variable determining the health of an [
estuary ](/wiki/Estuary "Estuary") , particularly from human-induced stresses.
Rapid flushing ensures that there is insufficient time for [ sediment
](/wiki/Sediment "Sediment") accumulation or [ dissolved oxygen
](/wiki/Dissolved_oxygen "Dissolved oxygen") depletion in the estuary; thus a
well flushed estuary is intrinsically more robust than a poorly flushed
estuary.  [1]  Residence time also affects other parameters such as [ heavy
metals ](/wiki/Heavy_metals "Heavy metals") , [ dissolved
](/wiki/Dissolution_\(chemistry\) "Dissolution \(chemistry\)") nutrients, [
suspended solids ](/wiki/Suspended_solids "Suspended solids") , and [ algal
](/wiki/Algal "Algal") blooms that may affect the health of estuaries.  [2]

